{"name":"Scotch Pancakes (BBC)","permalink":"scotch-pancakes","edit":"https://github.com/The-Silverwood-Institute/Recibase/tree/master/src/main/scala/se/reciba/api/recibase/recipes/DropPancakes.scala","source":"https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/drop-pancakes","description":null,"tagline":null,"notes":["You need very little butter to cook the pancakes. Too much and they won't cook properly"],"dated_notes":[],"tags":["Vegetarian","Scales","Pudding","Low Effort","Quick"],"inherited_tags":["Vegetarian-ish","Pescatarian"],"image":null,"ingredients_blocks":[{"name":null,"ingredients":[{"name":"Plain flour","quantity":"200g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Baking powder","quantity":"1/2 tbsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Fine salt","quantity":"1/2 tsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Golden caster sugar","quantity":"50g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Egg","quantity":"1","prep":"beaten","notes":null},{"name":"Milk","quantity":"200ml","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Butter","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":"for cooking"}]}],"method":["Sieve the plain flour into a bowl, then add the baking powder, golden caster sugar and fine salt.","Whisk the beaten egg and milk together in a jug, then pour into the bowl and whisk for a few minutes until you have a smooth, thick batter.","Add a little butter to a large frying pan.","Heat the pan over medium heat, and once hot drop 2 tablespoons of the batter into the pan to make small pancakes — you should be able to cook about 4-5 at a time.","Cook the pancakes for 2-3 minutes until the edges are set and bubbles rise in the centre. Flip and cook for another 2-3 minutes until golden brown and cooked through. Repeat with the remaining batter, adding more butter when needed.","Serve the drop pancakes topped with extra butter and a drizzle of maple syrup alongside seasonal fruit, if you like."]}